---
description: rules for writing unit tests
applyIntelligently: true
---

- Add or update tests in the same package as code under test.
- Name tests `Test<function>` or `Test<function>_<condition>` (e.g. `TestDo_Error`, `TestFixDimo_FixDest_DineIn`).
- Use `testify/require` for failures that should stop the test (errors, panics).
- Use `testify/assert` for value checks.
- If a package has multiple struct types with methods, use `testify/suite` to group the tests for those types.
- Do not access AWS services, RPC endpoints, or network; use mocks and fake credentials.
